# Allow-list: the build context is exactly what `cmake --preset release` needs to configure and
# build the `leta` target, and nothing else. Everything starts excluded; the build inputs are
# re-included below. A new top-level input the build reads needs a line here — the failure is a
# clean "No such file" at configure, never a silently fat context (M0-T7).
#
# Deliberately out:
#   .git             the commit reaches the build as --build-arg GIT_COMMIT (Dockerfile). Copying
#                    history into the builder would ship the whole repo per build for one string
#   build, data      host artefacts; the image builds from source only
#   docs, *.md       not build inputs. LICENSE and NOTICE stay in: they belong with the sources,
#                    and src/core/third_party/README.md carries tl::expected's licence
#   STATE.md, PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md, .env*, CMakeUserPresets.json — never leave the machine

*
!CMakeLists.txt
!CMakePresets.json
!cmake
!include
!src
!tests
!LICENSE
!NOTICE

# tests/ is needed to configure (add_subdirectory), but its data trees are read only by tests
# that this build never runs. Later rules win over the re-include above.
tests/data
tests/fuzz/corpus

# Host junk that a re-included tree may carry
**/build
**/.cache
**/*.swp
